' rs-matter error system — TARGET pattern (severed dependencies).
'
' Supersedes the earlier target that shared one InternalError across layers.
' Core principle: NO shared error type. Every layer owns a CLOSED enum, and
' every boundary crossing is an explicit, exhaustive conversion.
'
' Packages are labelled L0..L4 by dependency depth. A crate may only name
' types at its own level or BELOW.
'
' Arrows:
'   -->            exhaustive From impl, no `_` arm; `?` works
'   ..>            named conversion (not From), or "builds"
'   -[#B91C1C]->   conversion that loses context -> MUST log at the boundary

@startuml rs-matter-errors-target
title rs-matter error system — target pattern (severed error dependencies)

hide empty members
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam class {
  BorderColor #555555
  BackgroundColor #FCFCFC
  ArrowColor #333333
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #94A3B8
  FontStyle bold
}

' ======================================================================
' The principle
' ======================================================================

note as N_PRINCIPLE #FEF9C3
  **THE PRINCIPLE**

  There is no shared error type and no
  escape hatch. No `Other(Error)`, no
  `Internal(InternalError)`.

  Every layer owns a CLOSED enum listing
  only what that layer can actually fail
  with. A signature therefore states a real
  contract instead of "can fail with
  anything".

  Every boundary crossing is an explicit
  From impl with an **exhaustive match and
  no `_` arm**. Where the conversion loses
  context, it **logs at the boundary** --
  the pattern already used for foreign
  errors in rs-matter-utils today.
end note

' ======================================================================
' L0
' ======================================================================

package "L0  rs-matter-utils  (no internal deps)" #FEF2F2 {

  enum UtilsError {
    NoSpace
    BufferTooSmall
    InvalidState
    Utf8Fail
    RwLock
    StdIoError
    SysTimeFail
    ...
    ..
    fieldless -> **1 byte**
    ..
    **variant list TBD**
  }
}

note right of UtilsError
  Foreign errors (std::io, zbus, bluer,
  SystemTime, Utf8) convert IN here, and
  already log before discarding detail --
  see error.rs, four impls carrying the
  comment "we lose all context from the
  original error here".

  That established pattern IS the answer to
  "what replaces Other(Error)": log at
  origin, carry only a category.
end note

' ======================================================================
' L1 — below the IM layer: no status is reachable
' ======================================================================

package "L1  rs-matter-tlv, rs-matter-crypto, rs-matter-cert" #F1F5F9 {

  enum TlvError {
    TypeMismatch
    TagNotFound
    TruncatedPacket
    NoWriteSpace
    InvalidData
    ...
    ..
    fieldless -> **1 byte**
  }

  enum CryptoError {
    InvalidKeyLength
    InvalidAAD
    InvalidSignature
    ...
    ..
    fieldless -> **1 byte**
  }
}

UtilsError --> TlvError : From, exhaustive
UtilsError --> CryptoError : From, exhaustive

note bottom of TlvError
  These crates depend only on utils (+ macros),
  so they **cannot name IMStatusCode even in
  principle**. Their errors are necessarily
  pure faults -- which is correct for this
  tier.
end note

' ======================================================================
' L1 — the IM layer owns the spec status
' ======================================================================

package "L1  rs-matter-im-core  (the ONLY home of IMStatusCode)" #EFF6FF {

  enum IMStatusCode <<spec>> {
    Success = 0x00
    Failure = 0x01
    UnsupportedAccess = 0x7E
    ConstraintError = 0x87
    ...
    InvalidTransportType = 0xD1
    ..
    34 spec values
    ..
    **stays here.** No move to L0,
    no new L0 crate needed.
  }

  class Status <<spec: StatusIB>> {
    + status : IMStatusCode
    + cluster_status : Option<NonZeroU8>
  }

  class CmdStatus <<spec>> {
    + path : CmdPath
    + status : Status
    + command_ref : Option<u16>
  }

  class AttrStatus <<spec>> {
    + path : AttrPath
    + status : Status
  }

  Status *-- IMStatusCode
  CmdStatus *-- Status
  AttrStatus *-- Status
}

TlvError -[#B91C1C]-> IMStatusCode : From, exhaustive\n**logs**: a TLV fault has no\nwire meaning beyond Failure

' ======================================================================
' L2 — the first tier that can report a status
' ======================================================================

package "L2  rs-matter-dm-core" #ECFDF5 {

  enum DmCoreError {
    HandlerMissing
    DataverMismatch
    ListIndexInvalid
    ...
    == the ONLY payload variant ==
    Status(IMStatusCode)
    ..
    **1 byte** -- the fieldless
    variants fold into
    IMStatusCode's niche
  }

  class CmdDetails {
    + cluster_status : Cell<Option<NonZeroU8>>
    --
    + set_cluster_status(Option<NonZeroU8>)
    + cluster_status() : Option<NonZeroU8>
    + status(IMStatusCode) : Option<CmdStatus>
  }

  class AttrDetails {
    + cluster_status : Cell<Option<NonZeroU8>>
    --
    + set_cluster_status(Option<NonZeroU8>)
    + cluster_status() : Option<NonZeroU8>
    + status(IMStatusCode) : Option<AttrStatus>
  }
}

DmCoreError *-- IMStatusCode
TlvError --> DmCoreError : From, exhaustive
UtilsError --> DmCoreError : From, exhaustive
CmdDetails ..> CmdStatus : status()
AttrDetails ..> AttrStatus : status()

note right of DmCoreError
  **This is the shape that keeps 1 byte.**
  With the escape hatch gone, a layer that
  reports status has exactly ONE payload
  variant available -- Status(IMStatusCode) --
  so niche folding still applies.

  Previously this tier needed BOTH
  Status(..) and Internal(..), which is two
  payload variants and 2 bytes. Severing the
  dependency removes that cost rather than
  adding one.
end note

note bottom of AttrDetails
  **cluster_status staging: unchanged.**
  The cluster byte travels beside the Result,
  never inside the error. Reasons, in weight
  order:
   1. zero size cost
   2. the channels are not interchangeable
      on the wire and chip-tool certification
      enforces it (Scenes RecallScene)
   3. only PushAVStreamTransport has real
      spec-defined cluster codes
end note

